    {
      "file": "arch/TMS320C64x/TMS320C64xMapping.c",
      "function": "<file scope>",
      "line": null,
      "code": "static name_map insn_name_maps[] = {\n\t{ TMS320C64X_INS_INVALID, NULL },\n\n\t{ TMS320C64X_INS_ADD, \"add\" },\n\t{ TMS320C64X_INS_NOP, \"nop\" },\n};",
      "note": "The vulnerable TMS320C64x instruction-name table contains only three contiguous array elements even though `TMS320C64x_insn_name()` later indexes it by raw dense enum value. The embedded `name_map.id` fields do not create sparse array slots, so only indices 0, 1, and 2 are in bounds. The fix replaces the truncated table with one entry per enum value.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
